# Copy to `.env`. Loaded by `pnpm --filter @termspace/server start` via Node's
# own `--env-file-if-exists`, so there is no dotenv dependency and no import
# order to get wrong. Anything already exported in the shell wins over this file.
#
# Every value here has a default in `src/config/env.ts`. The two that bite on a
# dev box are the first two: the defaults are production-shaped and fail in ways
# that do not name themselves.

# Must equal the exact origin you load the UI from, or every WebSocket upgrade
# is refused with a bare 403 and no pane accepts a keystroke. `web` serves on
# 3002 unless PORT says otherwise.
TERMSPACE_ALLOWED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3002

# Must exist and be writable by the user running the server, or every project
# creation fails. Defaults to /srv/projects, which no dev box has.
TERMSPACE_PROJECT_ROOT=/home/you/projects

# TERMSPACE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# TERMSPACE_PORT=3001
# TERMSPACE_DATABASE_PATH=./data/termspace.db
# TERMSPACE_AUTH_SESSION_TTL_MS=28800000
